"helpHeading" = "CellCopyCleaner Help";
"helpText" = "## How to use\n1. Select cells in Microsoft Excel, or in Google Sheets opened in a browser (Google Chrome, Safari, Firefox).\n2. Press **⌥⌘C**. CellCopyCleaner sends Copy (⌘C) to the app, cleans the copied text and puts it back on the clipboard.\n3. Paste with ⌘V.\n- The result is shown briefly at the top of the screen and kept as “Last result” in the main window and at the top of the menu bar menu. On failure the clipboard is not changed.\n- ⌥⌘C is registered only while a target app is in front, so other apps keep their own ⌥⌘C. The front app is checked again right after the key press.\n\n## What is cleaned\n### Microsoft Excel\n- Formatting is removed (plain text).\n- A leading “‑” (U+2011 non-breaking hyphen) + run of “_” + one whitespace is removed at each line start (regex (?m)^‑_+\\s, case-insensitive).\n- Cells that Excel wraps in quotes (for example, cells with line breaks) lose the outer quotes, and \"\" inside becomes \" (judged per tab-separated cell).\n### Google Sheets (Chrome, Safari, Firefox)\nRemoves the quotes added when copying cells that contain line breaks, in this order, then writes plain text:\n1. Remove \" at the start of each line\n2. Remove \" at the end of each line\n3. Collapse runs of \" into one\n4. Replace ' (apostrophe) with \" (can be turned off in Settings > Target Apps)\n- Example: \"a(newline)b\" → a(newline)b, a\"\"b → a\"b\n- ※ Only line starts and ends are handled, so quotes of a cell in the middle of a tab-separated row may remain. This matches the original Keyboard Maestro macro.\n- ※ Cleaning runs only while a Google Sheets window (title contains “Google Sheets”, etc.) is in front. On other pages ⌥⌘C is passed on to the browser (for example, Chrome's Inspect Elements).\n\n## Restore\n- “Restore Original Copy” (main window, File menu, menu bar) puts back the content before cleaning (text, HTML, RTF). Images and other formats are not restored.\n- Nothing is restored after another copy. The content is kept in memory only and discarded on quit.\n\n## Settings\n- Startup & Background: launch at login (off by default), hide main window at startup, keep running after closing, show in menu bar, Accessibility status, restart and quit buttons.\n- Hotkey: enable or disable ⌥⌘C, pause until relaunch, change (Esc cancels recording), reset to default, success notification.\n- Target Apps: turn each of the four apps on or off (all on by default), apostrophe replacement.\n- About: version and links.\n- Open Settings with ⌘, and close it with ⌘W.\n\n## Hotkeys\n- **⌥⌘C**: copy and clean (only while a target app is in front).\n- Duplicates within this app and registration failures are shown in Settings. Not every conflict with other apps can be detected.\n\n## Accessibility permission\nNeeded to send ⌘C to the target app. Turn on CellCopyCleaner in System Settings > Privacy & Security > Accessibility. Settings > Startup & Background has a button that opens it. Without permission, ⌥⌘C shows the reason and does nothing.\n\n## Staying in the menu bar and quitting\n- The table icon in the menu bar offers the main window, Settings, Pause, Restore, Help and Quit. Hide the icon with Menu Bar Settings… in the app menu (the app keeps running).\n- Closing the window keeps the app running. Reopening it from the Dock or Finder shows the main window.\n- Quit with “Quit CellCopyCleaner” (app menu, menu bar, Settings > Startup & Background) or ⌘Q while the app is in front.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n- “Copy failed”: make sure cells are selected and you are not editing a cell. The run stops if the clipboard does not change within 1 second.\n- Nothing happens: check in Settings that the target app is on, the hotkey is enabled and not paused.\n- Still shown as not allowed after granting: restart the app. If that does not help, remove CellCopyCleaner from the list in System Settings and add it again.\n- If the Keyboard Maestro macro with ⌥⌘C is still enabled, both run. Disable the macro.\n\n## Privacy\nNo network communication (update checks stay off until an update feed is configured). Clipboard content is never logged or sent.\n\n## Uninstall\nDelete CellCopyCleaner from Applications. To remove settings, also delete ~/Library/Preferences/jp.dtp-transit.cellcopycleaner.plist, and remove the app from Login Items and the Accessibility list.";
